  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "First line in balmer series means transition from <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> to <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>. Now, <math><msup><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></msup></math> orbit of <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> has same energy as third orbit of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&prime;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&prime;</mi></math> atom & <math><msup><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></msup></math> orbit of <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> has same energy as second orbit of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&prime;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&prime;</mi></math> atom. So <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math> to <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math> transition in <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mi> </mi></math>would have same wavelength as first line in balmer series of <br/><br/><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>-spectrum.",
